MethodReferences : 
====================================

MethodReferences is one of the java 8 feature.

1.MethodReferences is a shorter way to writing of the lambda expression.
2.It generally used when the lambda is only calling an existing method.
3.It uses the doubke colon operator ::
	This operator is also known as method references operator.
4.We can access both static and non static methoda by using double operators.

For static method : 
className::static method
Demo::printmessgae;

For non-static method :
ObjectReference::method
Demo d=new Demo()
d::print

5.When calling method using ::
we do not provide the parenthesis for the method.
	eg:Demo::printmessage;